# PROPOSED FIX -- NOT APPLIED. quant_v7 paper bot: forward-evidence hygiene.
# Author: research/forward review, 2026-09-23. Diagnosis: reports/forward/PEAD_FORWARD_DIAGNOSIS.md
#
# What it changes (behaviour on a healthy day is unchanged: same candidates, same
# risk gate, same sizing, same fills):
#  1. earnings/ingestion.py: an endpoint that RAISES (DNS, timeout) is recorded in
#     df.attrs["primary_error"/"history_error"] instead of looking like an empty
#     answer; the frozen training-cache stand-in rows are tagged
#     date_source="cached_announced" instead of "announced".
#  2. bot/earnings_watcher.py: counts tickers whose fetches all raised
#     (fetch_errors) and exposes data_unreachable() (>= 90% of the universe);
#     newest_report ignores "cached_announced" rows, so the staleness check can no
#     longer report the training cache's 2025-06-26 as "the feed".
#  3. bot/run_cycle.py:
#     - one accurate alert when data is unreachable (replaces the misleading
#       "feed down" + "newest report 2025-06-26" pair of 2026-09-21 19:58 ET);
#       such a cycle is `degraded`: no entries evaluated, heartbeat NOT refreshed
#       (the watchdog then reports it), no marked_nav;
#     - marked_nav/unrealized_pnl are written only when EVERY open position was
#       priced (the 2026-09-21 19:58 record carried all 11 positions at cost);
#     - every cycle record carries provenance="live", started_at and code_sha256
#       (code + model fingerprint); every entry carries decided_at (wall clock at
#       the risk-gate decision, before the fill), decided_after_close, and the
#       exact inputs (EPS estimate/actual, surprise, trailing surprises, features)
#       -- Yahoo revises consensus after the fact, so they cannot be re-fetched.
#  4. bot/signal_pipeline.py: ScoredEvent carries `features` and `inputs`.
#  5. bot/execution.py: ledger records carry provenance ("live" by default),
#     price_source and decided_at. A record WITHOUT provenance predates this patch
#     and must be treated as "unknown", never as live.
#  6. live_backtest/backfill_missed_season.py: any future backfill writes
#     provenance="backfill" and the REAL write time (written_at), since its `ts`
#     is simulated.
#
# What it deliberately does NOT change: the entry convention. Every live entry is
# decided ~2.5-3.5 h AFTER the close it is filled at (launchd 15:42 PT = 18:42 ET).
# Fixing that changes the strategy (pre-close decision at the last price, or fill
# at the next official open) and needs a new registered spec version -- see
# PEAD_FORWARD_DIAGNOSIS.md section 7 and REPORT.md. This patch makes the lateness
# explicit per record (decided_after_close) instead of implicit.
#
# Tests: new tests/test_bot_forward_hygiene.py (7 tests: network failure vs empty
# answer; unreachable universe -> degraded, no stale alert, no heartbeat; one
# failing ticker is not an outage; partial marks -> no marked_nav; entry records
# decided_at <= fill ts, inputs, provenance). tests/test_earnings_outage_fallback.py
# updated for the "cached_announced" tag (2 assertions).
# Validated ONLY in a scratch copy of the repo (never in this tree): with the patch
# applied, tests/test_bot_forward_hygiene.py, test_earnings_outage_fallback.py,
# test_bot_earnings_watcher.py, test_bot_execution.py, test_bot_signal_pipeline.py,
# test_bot_run_cycle.py, test_backfill_missed_season.py, test_bot_performance.py,
# test_bot_position_manager.py, test_dashboard_backend.py: 125 passed, 6 skipped
# (skips = pre-existing network-dependent tests). Unpatched baseline of the first
# six files in the same copy: 50 passed, 4 skipped.
#
# To apply (the operator's decision; between cycles, i.e. not 15:40-16:45 PT on a weekday):
#   git apply --check reports/forward/proposed_fix.diff && git apply reports/forward/proposed_fix.diff
#   PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_bot_forward_hygiene.py tests/test_earnings_outage_fallback.py
